  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As we know that in alpha decay mass number reduced from for and the atomic number reduced by two</p><p>and in beta decay the mass number became unchange and atomic number increase from one</p><p>Change in <math><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math><br />Change in <math><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>TH</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>90</mn><mn>232</mn></mmultiscripts><mtable><mtr><mtd><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn><mi>&#946;</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mi>&#160;</mi><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>82</mn><mn>208</mn></mmultiscripts></math></p>",
